    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "** Detached bungalow **\n** Spacious rear garden **\n\nA warm welcome to 98 Monread Heights, an immaculate detached three bedroom bungalow that we at Byrne Malone are thrilled to be presenting to the market! Number 98 is situated on a quiet cul-de-sac of similar homes within this much sought-after development which is both family friendly and perfectly positioned close to an abundance of local amenities. Notably, it is just a short stroll to Monread Park and both Sallins/Naas train station and the N7 interchange are within easy reach, making it particularly appealing to commuters traveling to Dublin.\n\nMeasuring 91 sqm, this lovely home is beautifully appointed throughout and comes to the market recently painted and floored, and boasting a spacious rear garden, presenting a lovely opportunity for a budding gardener to make their own.\n\nUpon entering, you are welcomed by a bright hallway which leads to a spacious living room complete with a cast iron wood stove providing a lovely focal point for the space. Beyond here you have the kitchen which is fully fitted with cream shaker style base and eye level units with double patio doors leading to the light filled conservatory which opens into the garden.\nBack inside, off the hallway there are three generous bedrooms, two overlooking the back garden the main bedroom overlooking the front. The property was extended in 2005, so where the original bathroom was, is now a spacious storage area that would make a great utility space or similar, and this leads to elegantly tiled shower room with pristine sanitary ware and vaulted ceiling bringing light and height to this relaxing space.\n\nOutside the house is approached by a driveway with it own off street parking, flanked by neat lawn to the front. A secure side passage then leads to the back garden which measures 42ft by 38 ft approx., The garden is safely enclosed and boasts a neatly kept lawn, perfect for children to play and offering a charming blank canvas for any budding gardener to cultivate!\nMonread Heights is ideally located on the edge of Naas town and within walking distance to local Spar and Applegreen shops and Naas town also. \n\nNaas needs little introduction, with an enviable host of amenities including shops such as Dunnes Stores and Tesco Express and larger retailers at The Globe and Newhall Retail Parks, schools, bars and restaurants, hotels, cinema and numerous sporting facilities such as Punchestown racecourse. Sports are well catered for with a host of golf courses to choose from, Naas Rugby Club, Naas GAA and Naas Tennis club also. The M7 motorway and Sallins/Naas Train Station are both in close proximity offering quick & easy commuting.\n\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to acquire a lovely detached home all one on level with a garden to make your own, and we highly recommend early viewing!"
      },
